{
  "$schema": "./schema/minigame.schema.json",
  "design_notes": [
    "One entry per block of design section 10.5, in catalog order (MG-08b before MG-08, MG-10a before MG-10, as printed). when_key, detail_key, success_key and reward_summary_key are the When, How to play, Success and Boost lines as printed; how_to_play_key is the one-sentence instruction that rule 4 of 10.1 asks for, condensed from the How to play line.",
    "params holds the numbers of the Success line. Suffix convention: _min means at least (≥), _max at most (≤), _below strictly less than (<); fractions are 0 to 1 (85% is 0.85). Where the Success line has no number (MG-09, MG-12, MG-18, MG-19, MG-20, MG-23, MG-26, MG-27, MG-28, MG-29) nothing is stored: the bands and gates are minigame tuning the design leaves open.",
    "rewards: a reward with boost pays the catalog amount of data/boosts.json for the tier earned (Platinum pays the Gold column). A reward limited to tiers applies only there. Rewards the design states without a number are flags with a text; Core must implement or deliberately ignore each flag. boost_size small marks \"small\" boosts, whose size the design leaves open.",
    "fact_key is the one-line fact of the result screen (25 words or fewer, 12.1). For the 22 minigames whose fact is in the fact bank it is the text key of that fact and facts holds its ID; for the other ten (MG-03, MG-05, MG-06, MG-08b, MG-09, MG-10, MG-20, MG-24, MG-27, MG-28) the bank of 12.4 has no entry, so the text is stored under the minigame. Section 12.4 asks that new facts be added to the bank with a source before release.",
    "accessibility: section 16 requires a Relaxed mode and a One-Button alternative for every timing minigame and rule 8 of 10.1 a one-button or no-timing mode for every minigame, but the design describes neither for any minigame. Both notes of every entry are proposals by the data author and give no numbers; hold-to-press can always switch to toggle.",
    "triggers follow the When line. Event names (staging, ground_station_pass, debris_conjunction, alarms, eclipse, life_support_event, science_target_pass, blackout_end, mission_failure, major_anomaly) are markers Core must raise; debris_conjunction, alarms and eclipse are the possible events of flight phase F8 in data/flight_phases.json.",
    "flight_phases holds flight-phase IDs (F0 to F14), facts holds fact IDs (F01 to F40); the two kinds never share a field.",
    "Durations are play time. The types of MG-28 and MG-30 are \"Cooperative\", which is not one of the four types of 10.2."
  ],
